cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Novelty vs. contamination in eDNA reads from a genomic language
  model's per-base surprise
message: If you use this software or dataset, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Maia
    family-names: Kaplan
    affiliation: Universidad de Buenos Aires / IQUIBICEN
repository-code: 'https://github.com/__GH_USER__/evo2-edna-novelty'
abstract: >-
  Code and data for distinguishing true evolutionary novelty from
  contamination artefacts in hard-to-classify 313 bp COI eDNA reads,
  using per-base negative log-likelihood profiles from the Evo2 (7B)
  genomic language model. Includes a graded novelty simulation across
  five taxonomic ranks, five contamination mechanisms, cluster-atomic
  cross-validation, and a scalar-to-MLP capacity ladder.
keywords:
  - environmental DNA
  - metabarcoding
  - genomic language model
  - Evo2
  - perplexity
  - contamination detection
  - novelty detection
license: MIT
